   nd_bind: recursion on the result of applying a stored function
   (m_act st), not a subterm -> fuel.
   nd_foldlM: structural on its list argument -> automatic.
   liftND/liftAction: genuinely cyclic mutual pair, recursion through
   stored-function application -> fuel both (all-or-none).
   FUEL ARC (2026-09-03, docs/2026-09-02_fuel-arc-design.md section 1.2):
   the fuel-zero arm of every ND-typed fueled worker is the DISTINGUISHED,
   kernel-transparent kill `NDkilled (Error0 CerbFuel.fuelExhaustedLoc
   CerbFuel.fuelExhaustedMsg)` (= CerbND.fuelExhaustedKill) with NO opaque
   `fuelExhausted` wrapper around the monadic value — exhaustion is a typed
   outcome the kernel can recognise (the `_zero` lemmas in CerbND.lean hold
   by rfl), printed by Main as `Error {msg: "lem: fuel exhausted"}` and
   classified FUEL by the harnesses. The atom `fuelExhaustedLoc` is a pure
   opaque (CerbFuel.lean, imported via the extra_import above). liftAction
   returns nd_action, so its arm is the curried action-shaped value. === -/
